I left out both of the operations team's additions, because the node's authority doesn't allow them:

- **Log file:** the `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem capability, and the target has no WASI.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the HTTPClient allowlist, so the host would trap the call. The input's text would also be sent to an unlisted service.

If operations needs either one, the graph would have to grant it explicitly, for example a log or state capability and a widened allowlist.

Subscription URLs whose host is outside the allowlist are recorded as failures instead of calling the host, since a refused request would trap the whole run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

const ALLOWED_HOSTS: [&str; 4] = [
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

fn host_allowed(url: &str) -> bool {
    let rest = if let Some(r) = url.strip_prefix("https://") {
        r
    } else if let Some(r) = url.strip_prefix("http://") {
        r
    } else {
        return false;
    };
    let end = rest
        .find(|c| c == '/' || c == '?' || c == '#')
        .unwrap_or(rest.len());
    let authority = &rest[..end];
    if authority.contains('@') {
        return false;
    }
    let host = authority.split(':').next().unwrap_or("").to_ascii_lowercase();
    ALLOWED_HOSTS.iter().any(|h| *h == host)
}

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if !host_allowed(&url) {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "host not in allowlist".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

